==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|vai}}
* {{rhymes|ɑi|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|[ʋɑi]|lang=fi}}

===Conjunction===
{{fi-con}}

# {{context|lang=fi|coordinating; in question clauses}} [[or]]
#: ''Onko se suuri '''vai''' pieni?''
#:: ''Is it big '''or''' small?''

====Usage notes====

While it is often said that {{term|tai|lang=fi}} is to be used in affirmative clauses and {{term||lang=fi|vai}} is to be used in question clauses, a more precise difference is that {{term||tai|lang=fi}} is an [[inclusive or]], while {{term||lang=fi|vai}} is an [[exclusive or]]. For instance, while {{term||Söitkö sinä leivän '''tai''' hedelmät?|lang=fi}} and {{term||lang=fi|Söitkö sinä leivän '''vai''' hedelmät?}} are both correct, the former asks in a yes or no question, whether you ate either bread or fruit or not, while the latter asks which you ate, the bread or the fruit.

====See also====
* {{l|fi|tai}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|fi|iva}},  {{l|fi|via}}

[[Category:Finnish coordinating conjunctions]]

